{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "ccc225a2-d682-4627-9f77-5d44f27c99a1",
		"name": "LMS Mentoring API",
		"description": "Postman collection for Learning Management System (Mentoring Project)\n\n## Authentication\n\n### Local Development\n- Use Basic Auth with credentials: user/password or manager/secret\n\n### Cloud (SAP BTP)\n- Use OAuth2 Bearer Token from XSUAA\n- First run 'Get XSUAA Token' request to obtain access token\n- All API requests will automatically use the token\n\n## Pagination\n\nGET all endpoints support pagination via query parameters:\n- `page`: Page number (0-indexed, default: 0)\n- `size`: Page size (default: 20)\n- `sort`: Sort field and direction (e.g., `title,asc` or `createdAt,desc`)\n\nExample: `GET /api/v1/students?page=0&size=10&sort=lastName,asc`\n\n## Localization\n\nStudents have a `locale` field for email notification language preference:\n- Supported: `en`, `de`, `ru`\n- Default: `en`\n\n## Multitenancy\n\nThe application supports SAP BTP multitenancy:\n- Access via Approuter: `https://{tenant-subdomain}-lms-approuter.cfapps.us10-001.hana.ondemand.com`\n- Admin endpoint `/api/v1/application-info` requires ADMIN role\n- SaaS Registry callbacks at `/callback/v1.0/`",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "6593295",
		"_collection_link": "https://interstellar-star-3717.postman.co/workspace/LMS-Mentoring~12b651dc-1296-4e99-b81d-a41d8e64b088/collection/6593295-ccc225a2-d682-4627-9f77-5d44f27c99a1?action=share&source=collection_link&creator=6593295"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Authentication (Cloud)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get XSUAA Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"if (jsonData.access_token) {",
									"    pm.environment.set(\"xsuaa_access_token\", jsonData.access_token);",
									"    console.log(\"Access token saved to xsuaa_access_token\");",
									"    console.log(\"Token expires in: \" + jsonData.expires_in + \" seconds\");",
									"} else {",
									"    console.error(\"No access_token in response\");",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "basic",
							"basic": [
								{
									"key": "username",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_clientid}}",
									"type": "string"
								},
								{
									"key": "password",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_clientsecret}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "client_credentials",
									"type": "text"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{xsuaa_url}}/oauth/token",
							"host": [
								"{{xsuaa_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"oauth",
								"token"
							]
						},
						"description": "Gets an OAuth2 access token from XSUAA for API authentication.\n\n**The token is automatically saved to `xsuaa_access_token` environment variable.**\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Get XSUAA credentials from your app:\n   ```\n   cf env learning-management-system | grep -A 50 'lms-xsuaa'\n   ```\n\n2. Set these environment variables:\n   - `xsuaa_clientid`: clientid from credentials\n   - `xsuaa_clientsecret`: clientsecret from credentials\n   - `xsuaa_url`: url from credentials (e.g., https://xxx.authentication.us10.hana.ondemand.com)\n\n3. Run this request to get a token\n\n4. All other API requests will use the token automatically"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Token (Decode JWT)",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "https://jwt.io/#debugger-io?token={{xsuaa_access_token}}",
							"protocol": "https",
							"host": [
								"jwt",
								"io"
							],
							"hash": "debugger-io?token={{xsuaa_access_token}}"
						},
						"description": "Open jwt.io to decode and verify your XSUAA token.\n\nNote: This just opens the URL - you can paste your token at jwt.io to see its contents."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Subscriber Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"if (jsonData.access_token) {",
									"    pm.environment.set(\"subscriber_access_token\", jsonData.access_token);",
									"    console.log(\"Subscriber access token saved to subscriber_access_token\");",
									"    console.log(\"Token expires in: \" + jsonData.expires_in + \" seconds\");",
									"    ",
									"    // Decode JWT to show tenant info",
									"    var parts = jsonData.access_token.split('.');",
									"    if (parts.length === 3) {",
									"        var payload = JSON.parse(atob(parts[1]));",
									"        console.log(\"Tenant ID (zid): \" + payload.zid);",
									"        if (payload.ext_attr) {",
									"            console.log(\"Subdomain: \" + payload.ext_attr.zdn);",
									"            console.log(\"Subaccount ID: \" + payload.ext_attr.subaccountid);",
									"        }",
									"    }",
									"} else {",
									"    console.error(\"No access_token in response\");",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "basic",
							"basic": [
								{
									"key": "username",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_clientid}}",
									"type": "string"
								},
								{
									"key": "password",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_clientsecret}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "client_credentials",
									"type": "text"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "https://{{subscriber_subdomain}}.authentication.{{cf_region}}.hana.ondemand.com/oauth/token",
							"protocol": "https",
							"host": [
								"{{subscriber_subdomain}}",
								"authentication",
								"{{cf_region}}",
								"hana",
								"ondemand",
								"com"
							],
							"path": [
								"oauth",
								"token"
							]
						},
						"description": "Gets an OAuth2 token using the **subscriber's subdomain**.\n\n**Key Concept:** In SaaS multitenancy with XSUAA broker plan:\n- Same client ID and secret work for all tenants\n- The **subdomain in the URL** determines which tenant the token is for\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Set `subscriber_subdomain` to your subscriber's subdomain\n2. Set `cf_region` (e.g., 'us10' for US East)\n3. Use same `xsuaa_clientid` and `xsuaa_clientsecret`\n\n**Example URLs:**\n- Provider: `https://0658761dtrial.authentication.us10.hana.ondemand.com`\n- Subscriber: `https://lms-subscriber.authentication.us10.hana.ondemand.com`\n\n**The token's `zid` claim will contain the subscriber's tenant ID!**"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "XSUAA OAuth2 authentication for SAP BTP Cloud Foundry.\n\n## How to use:\n\n1. Set environment variables from XSUAA service binding:\n   - xsuaa_clientid\n   - xsuaa_clientsecret\n   - xsuaa_url\n\n2. Run 'Get XSUAA Token' request\n\n3. The token is automatically saved and used by all API requests"
		},
		{
			"name": "Multitenancy (Admin)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Tenant Context",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_access_token}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{backend_host}}/api/v1/tenant-context",
							"host": [
								"{{backend_host}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"tenant-context"
							]
						},
						"description": "Returns current tenant context from the JWT token.\n\n**Use this to verify which tenant is making the request.**\n\n**Response includes:**\n- `tenantId`: The zone/tenant ID (zid claim) - different for each subscriber\n- `subdomain`: The subscriber's subdomain\n- `subaccountId`: The subscriber's subaccount ID\n- `isProvider`: true if token is from provider tenant\n- `isSubscriber`: true if token is from subscriber tenant\n\n**Testing Multitenancy:**\n1. Get token from provider (normal XSUAA token)\n2. Call this endpoint - should show isProvider: true\n3. Get token from subscriber XSUAA\n4. Call this endpoint - should show isSubscriber: true with different tenantId"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Tenant Context (Subscriber)",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{xsuaa_access_token}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{subscriber_host}}/api/v1/tenant-context",
							"host": [
								"{{subscriber_host}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"tenant-context"
							]
						},
						"description": "Returns tenant context via subscriber route.\n\n**Compare the response with provider tenant context to see the difference.**"
					},
					"response": []
				},
